IMPORT prelude

-- Reciprocal Enforcement of Foreign Judgments Act 1959 (Singapore) -- which foreign judgments the Act reaches (ss 2, 2A, 3),
-- applying to register one in the General Division of the High Court and for how much (s 4), setting the registration aside
-- (ss 5, 6), the bar on suing on the judgment instead (s 7), the conclusive effect of a foreign judgment (s 11), countries
-- denied enforcement for want of reciprocity (s 12), and certificates for enforcing a Singapore judgment abroad (s 13).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (the deposit's page furniture reads "version in force from 1/3/2023"),
-- as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/REFJA1959.txt. The cover says the revised edition "incorporates all amendments
-- up to and including 1 December 2021"; later annotations shown are S 26/2022 (wef 13/01/2022), Act 25 of 2021 (wef
-- 01/04/2022) and the repeal of Part 2 by Act 24 of 2019 (wef 01/03/2023). Section numbers follow the body (s 1 short title,
-- s 2 interpretation, s 2A application); the arrangement at the top of the deposit is out of step with it.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0045 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario
-- has asked a sharper question yet. The Act is short, so nearly all of its operative provisions are here. Not encoded:
-- which countries and courts are gazetted under s 3 (no order was retrieved), the Rules of Court and Family Justice Rules
-- (s 8: security for costs, the matters to be proved, the period for applying to set aside), the rate of interest, and
-- s 11(3) (recognition that would have applied before 21 March 1959).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Reciprocal Enforcement of Foreign Judgments Act 1959 -- registration`

§§ `2 -- money and non-money judgments`

-- s 2(1): "'money judgment' means a judgment under which a sum of money is payable, NOT being a sum payable in respect of taxes
-- or other charges of a similar nature or in respect of a fine or other penalty"; "'non-money judgment' means a judgment that
-- is not a money judgment, but DOES NOT INCLUDE a judgment under which a sum of money is payable in respect of taxes ... or
-- in respect of a fine or other penalty". A "judgment" includes interlocutory and final judgments in civil proceedings,
-- compensation orders in criminal proceedings, consent judgments and orders, and judicial settlements.
--
-- A judgment for taxes, a fine or a penalty is therefore neither a money judgment nor a non-money judgment.
DECLARE Payment IS ONE OF
    `a sum of money for damages, a debt or compensation`
    `a sum of money for taxes or similar charges`
    `a sum of money as a fine or penalty`
    `no sum of money`

DECLARE JudgmentKind IS ONE OF
    `a money judgment`
    `a non-money judgment`
    `neither a money nor a non-money judgment`

GIVEN `the payment` IS A Payment
GIVETH A JudgmentKind
`the kind of judgment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the payment`
    WHEN `a sum of money for damages, a debt or compensation` THEN `a money judgment`
    WHEN `no sum of money` THEN `a non-money judgment`
    OTHERWISE `neither a money nor a non-money judgment`

-- s 2(2): "'action in personam' shall not be deemed to include any matrimonial cause or any proceedings in connection with"
-- (a) matrimonial matters; (b) administration of the estates of deceased persons; (c) bankruptcy; (d) winding up of companies,
-- including VCCs and sub-funds; (e) lunacy; (f) guardianship of infants.
DECLARE ActionKind IS ONE OF
    `a claim in contract or tort`
    `a matrimonial cause`
    `administration of a deceased person's estate`
    `bankruptcy`
    `winding up of a company`
    `guardianship of infants`
    `an action about immovable property`
    `an action in rem about movable property`

GIVEN `the action` IS AN ActionKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the action is an action in personam` IF
    CONSIDER `the action`
    WHEN `a claim in contract or tort` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `2A, 3 -- judgments to which Part 1 applies`

-- s 2A: the Act "does not apply to any judgment which may be recognised or enforced in Singapore under the Choice of Court
-- Agreements Act 2016".
-- s 3(1): the Minister, if satisfied that "substantial reciprocity of treatment will be assured", may by order in the Gazette
-- apply Part 1 to a foreign country, name its recognised courts, and specify the judgments. (2): a judgment of a recognised
-- court is within the subsection if "(a) it is given AFTER the coming into operation of the order; and (b) it is final and
-- conclusive as between the parties to it, UNLESS it is an interlocutory judgment". (4) excluded: "(a) a judgment given by
-- that court on appeal from a court that is not a recognised court"; (b) a judgment or instrument treated as that court's but
-- "given or made in another foreign country"; (c) a judgment in proceedings to enforce another foreign country's judgment.
-- (5): a judgment is final and conclusive "even though (a) an appeal may be pending against it; or (b) it may still be
-- subject to appeal".
DECLARE Judgment HAS
    `is of a recognised court and of a description specified in a section 3 order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was given after the order came into operation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is final and conclusive between the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is interlocutory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an appeal is pending or still possible` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was given on appeal from a court that is not recognised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was given or made in another foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `enforces a judgment of another foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `may be enforced under the Choice of Court Agreements Act 2016` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 1 applies to the judgment` IF
        (NOT `the judgment`'s `may be enforced under the Choice of Court Agreements Act 2016`)
    AND `the judgment`'s `is of a recognised court and of a description specified in a section 3 order`
    AND `the judgment`'s `was given after the order came into operation`
    AND (    `the judgment`'s `is final and conclusive between the parties`
         OR  `the judgment`'s `is interlocutory`)
    AND (NOT `the judgment`'s `was given on appeal from a court that is not recognised`)
    AND (NOT `the judgment`'s `was given or made in another foreign country`)
    AND (NOT `the judgment`'s `enforces a judgment of another foreign country`)

§§ `4(1)-(4) -- whether the judgment may be registered`

-- s 4(1): a judgment creditor "may apply to the General Division of the High Court at any time -- (a) within 6 years after
-- the date of the judgment; or (b) where there have been proceedings by way of appeal against the judgment, after the date of
-- the last judgment given in those proceedings". (Read here, as an INFERENCE, as six years running from the last appeal
-- judgment where there was an appeal; the text does not repeat "within 6 years" in (b). "Within 6 years" is read as at most
-- six years.)
-- (2): on proof of the prescribed matters the court "shall ... order the judgment to be registered".
-- (3): not registered if at the date of the application "(a) it has been wholly satisfied; (b) it has been discharged; or (c)
-- it could not be enforced in the country of the original court".
-- (4): a non-money judgment may be registered ONLY if enforcement "would be just and convenient"; if not, the court "may make
-- an order for the registration of such amount as it considers to be the monetary equivalent of the relief".
DECLARE Application HAS
    `years since the judgment, or since the last appeal judgment` IS A NUMBER
    `wholly satisfied at the application date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `discharged at the application date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `enforceable in the country of the original court at the application date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court finds enforcement just and convenient` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Outcome IS ONE OF
    `registered`
    `the monetary equivalent of the relief may be registered instead`
    `not registered`

GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment, `the application` IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is within section 4(1) and (3)` IF
        `Part 1 applies to the judgment` `the judgment`
    AND `the application`'s `years since the judgment, or since the last appeal judgment` AT MOST 6
    AND (NOT `the application`'s `wholly satisfied at the application date`)
    AND (NOT `the application`'s `discharged at the application date`)
    AND `the application`'s `enforceable in the country of the original court at the application date`

GIVEN `the judgment` IS A Judgment, `the payment` IS A Payment, `the application` IS AN Application
GIVETH AN Outcome
`the outcome of the application` MEANS
    IF NOT `the application is within section 4(1) and (3)` `the judgment` `the application`
    THEN `not registered`
    ELSE IF `the kind of judgment` `the payment` EQUALS `a non-money judgment`
         THEN IF `the application`'s `the court finds enforcement just and convenient`
              THEN `registered`
              ELSE `the monetary equivalent of the relief may be registered instead`
         ELSE `registered`

§§ `4(5), (6), (9), (11) -- the sum registered`

-- s 4(5): if a money judgment "awards damages (including exemplary or punitive damages) that are in excess of compensation
-- for the actual loss or harm suffered", it "may only be registered for the amount of the compensation". (6): the court must
-- take into account whether, and how far, the damages "serve to cover costs and expenses relating to the proceedings".
-- (9): if "partly satisfied", registered "only in respect of the balance remaining payable".
-- (11): "In addition to any sum of money payable under the judgment ... (including any interest which by the law of the country
-- of the original court becomes due under the judgment up to the time of registration) ... the judgment MUST be registered for
-- the reasonable costs of and incidental to registration, including the costs of obtaining a certified copy".
--
-- `the compensation as assessed` is the court's figure under s 4(5) and (6), including any part of the award that covers the
-- costs of the foreign proceedings. The ORDER in which the cap and the part payment are applied is an INFERENCE: the text does
-- not say how (5) and (9) combine. Here the award is capped first and payments then deducted.
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

DECLARE MoneyClaim HAS
    `sum awarded` IS A NUMBER
    `compensation as assessed` IS A NUMBER
    `already paid` IS A NUMBER
    `interest due under the original law up to registration` IS A NUMBER
    `reasonable costs of registration` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the claim` IS A MoneyClaim
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum registered` MEANS
        `the lesser of` (`the claim`'s `sum awarded`) (`the claim`'s `compensation as assessed`)
    MINUS `the claim`'s `already paid`
    PLUS `the claim`'s `interest due under the original law up to registration`
    PLUS `the claim`'s `reasonable costs of registration`

§§ `4(7), (8) -- effect of registration and when it can be enforced`

-- s 4(7): a registered judgment has "the same force and effect" for enforcement, carries interest, and is under the court's
-- control "as if the judgment had been a judgment originally given in the registering court and entered on the date of
-- registration".
-- (8): "An enforcement order MUST NOT be issued to enforce a judgment so long as ... it is competent for any party to make an
-- application to have the registration of the judgment set aside or, where such application is made, until after the
-- application has been finally determined."
GIVEN `registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `the period to apply to set aside is still running` IS A BOOLEAN, `a set-aside application is undetermined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an enforcement order may issue` IF
        `registered`
    AND (NOT `the period to apply to set aside is still running`)
    AND (NOT `a set-aside application is undetermined`)

§§ `5, 6 -- setting the registration aside`

-- s 5(1)(a): the registration "SHALL be set aside" if the court is satisfied (i) the judgment is not one to which Part 1
-- applies "or was registered in contravention of sections 3 and 4"; (ii) the original courts "had no jurisdiction"; (iii) the
-- defendant debtor did not receive notice "in sufficient time to enable him to defend ... and did not appear" (even if duly
-- served under the foreign law); (iv) "obtained by fraud"; (v) enforcement "would be contrary to public policy" in Singapore;
-- (vi) the rights are "not vested in the person by whom the application for registration was made".
-- (b) "MAY be set aside" if the matter had already been the subject of "a final and conclusive judgment by a court having
-- jurisdiction"; (c) MAY be set aside if the notice of registration "had not been served ... or ... was defective".
-- s 6(1): on proof that "an appeal is pending, or that he is entitled and intends to appeal", the court "if it thinks fit, MAY"
-- set aside or adjourn.
--
-- Wholly satisfied, discharged, unenforceable at origin, and registered for the whole sum despite part payment are breaches of
-- s 4 and so fall under (a)(i). The Act lists no ground that the foreign court got the merits wrong.
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `not a judgment to which Part 1 applies`
    `already wholly satisfied when registration was applied for`
    `already discharged when registration was applied for`
    `registered for the whole sum despite part payment`
    `not enforceable in the original country when registration was applied for`
    `the original court had no jurisdiction`
    `the defendant had no timely notice and did not appear`
    `obtained by fraud`
    `contrary to Singapore public policy`
    `the applicant did not hold the rights under the judgment`
    `an earlier final judgment on the same matter`
    `the notice of registration was not served or was defective`
    `an appeal is pending or intended`
    `the foreign court decided the merits wrongly`

DECLARE Effect IS ONE OF
    `must be set aside`
    `may be set aside`
    `no ground to set aside`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH AN Effect
`the effect of the ground` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `an earlier final judgment on the same matter` THEN `may be set aside`
    WHEN `the notice of registration was not served or was defective` THEN `may be set aside`
    WHEN `an appeal is pending or intended` THEN `may be set aside`
    WHEN `the foreign court decided the merits wrongly` THEN `no ground to set aside`
    OTHERWISE `must be set aside`

-- s 5(2): (1)(c) "does not prevent the subsequent registration of a judgment the registration of which has been previously set
-- aside solely under that provision". s 6(2): setting aside under s 6(1), or "solely for the reason that the judgment was not
-- ... enforceable in the country of the original court", "shall not prejudice a further application to register". s 6(3):
-- where set aside solely because a partly satisfied judgment was registered for the whole sum, the court "SHALL, on the
-- application of the judgment creditor, order judgment to be registered for the balance".
-- For the other grounds the Act says nothing either way; FALSE below means only that the Act does not expressly preserve it.
GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act expressly preserves registering again` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `the notice of registration was not served or was defective` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an appeal is pending or intended` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `not enforceable in the original country when registration was applied for` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `registered for the whole sum despite part payment` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `5(3), (4) -- when the original court had jurisdiction`

-- s 5(3)(a): in an action in personam, jurisdiction is deemed if the defendant debtor (i) "submitted to the jurisdiction of that
-- court by voluntarily appearing", OTHER THAN to protect or release seized property, contest the jurisdiction, or invite the
-- court to decline it; (ii) was a claimant or counterclaimed; (iii) had "before the commencement of the proceedings agreed ...
-- to submit"; (iv) was resident, or as a body corporate had its principal place of business, in that country when the
-- proceedings were instituted; (v) had an office or place of business there and the proceedings concerned "a transaction
-- effected through or at that office or place". (b) immovable property, or an action in rem over movable property: if the
-- property was situate in that country. (c) any other action: "if the jurisdiction of the original court is recognised by the
-- law of the registering court".
-- (4) NOTWITHSTANDING (3), no jurisdiction "(a) if the subject matter ... was immovable property outside the country"; (b)
-- "except in the cases mentioned in subsection (3)(a)(i), (ii) and (iii) and (c)", if the proceedings were "contrary to an
-- agreement under which the dispute ... was to be settled otherwise than by proceedings in the courts of the country"; (c) if
-- the defendant was entitled to immunity under public international law "and did not submit".
-- Treating (3)(a)(i)-(iii) as the meaning of "submit" in (4)(c) is an INFERENCE.
DECLARE Proceedings HAS
    `the action` IS AN ActionKind
    `appeared voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appeared only to protect property, contest jurisdiction or ask the court to decline` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was claimant or counterclaimed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had agreed beforehand to submit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was resident or had principal place of business there` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had an office there and the transaction went through it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the property was situate in that country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `concerned immovable property outside that country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `breached an agreement to settle the dispute elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was entitled to immunity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Singapore law recognises the jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the proceedings` IS A Proceedings
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the debtor submitted` IF
        (    `the proceedings`'s `appeared voluntarily`
         AND (NOT `the proceedings`'s `appeared only to protect property, contest jurisdiction or ask the court to decline`))
    OR  `the proceedings`'s `was claimant or counterclaimed`
    OR  `the proceedings`'s `had agreed beforehand to submit`

GIVEN `the proceedings` IS A Proceedings
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the original court is deemed to have had jurisdiction` IF
        (NOT `the proceedings`'s `concerned immovable property outside that country`)
    AND (NOT (`the proceedings`'s `was entitled to immunity` AND (NOT `the debtor submitted` `the proceedings`)))
    AND IF `the action is an action in personam` (`the proceedings`'s `the action`)
        THEN     `the debtor submitted` `the proceedings`
             OR  (    (    `the proceedings`'s `was resident or had principal place of business there`
                       OR  `the proceedings`'s `had an office there and the transaction went through it`)
                  AND (NOT `the proceedings`'s `breached an agreement to settle the dispute elsewhere`))
        ELSE IF     `the proceedings`'s `the action` EQUALS `an action about immovable property`
                OR  `the proceedings`'s `the action` EQUALS `an action in rem about movable property`
             THEN     `the proceedings`'s `the property was situate in that country`
                  AND (NOT `the proceedings`'s `breached an agreement to settle the dispute elsewhere`)
             ELSE `the proceedings`'s `Singapore law recognises the jurisdiction`

§§ `7, 12 -- suing on the judgment instead`

-- s 7(1): "No proceedings for the recovery of a sum payable under a foreign judgment, being a judgment to which this Part
-- applies, OTHER THAN proceedings by way of registration of the judgment, shall be entertained by any court in Singapore."
-- (2): where the order came into operation before its Gazette publication, (1) applies "only to proceedings commenced ... on or
-- after the date the relevant order is published in the Gazette".
-- s 12(2): where the Minister has applied s 12 to a country for treating Singapore judgments "substantially less favourable[y]",
-- "no proceedings shall be entertained ... for the recovery of any sum alleged to be payable under judgment given in a court
-- of" that country, except so far as the order otherwise directs.
GIVEN `Part 1 applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `the order operated before Gazette publication` IS A BOOLEAN, `the action began before Gazette publication` IS A BOOLEAN, `section 12 applies to the country` IS A BOOLEAN, `the section 12 order directs otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Singapore court may hear an ordinary action on the judgment` IF
        (    (NOT `Part 1 applies`)
         OR  (`the order operated before Gazette publication` AND `the action began before Gazette publication`))
    AND (    (NOT `section 12 applies to the country`)
         OR  `the section 12 order directs otherwise`)

§§ `11 -- conclusive effect`

-- s 11(1): a judgment to which Part 1 applies, "or would have applied if a sum of money had been payable thereunder, whether or
-- not it can be or is registered, shall be recognised ... as conclusive between the parties ... in all proceedings founded on
-- the same cause of action and may be relied on by way of defence or counterclaim".
-- (2): not where the registration has been set aside, or (if unregistered) would have been, "on some ground OTHER THAN (i) that a
-- sum of money was not payable under the judgment; (ii) that the judgment had been wholly or partly satisfied; or (iii) that
-- at the date of the application the judgment could not be enforced in the country of the original court".
-- (No current s 5 ground is worded as "a sum of money was not payable"; that limb is not modelled.)
GIVEN `Part 1 applies or would if money were payable` IS A BOOLEAN, `set aside, or would be` IS A BOOLEAN, `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the judgment is conclusive between the parties` IF
        `Part 1 applies or would if money were payable`
    AND (    (NOT `set aside, or would be`)
         OR  CONSIDER `the ground`
             WHEN `already wholly satisfied when registration was applied for` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `registered for the whole sum despite part payment` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `not enforceable in the original country when registration was applied for` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `the foreign court decided the merits wrongly` THEN TRUE
             OTHERWISE FALSE)

§§ `13 -- enforcing a Singapore judgment abroad`

-- s 13(1): where a judgment has been given in a Singapore court and the creditor "desires to enforce the judgment in a foreign
-- country to which Part 1 applies", the registrar, on application and payment of the prescribed fee, "is to issue" certified
-- copies of the pleadings, order of court and written grounds, with a certificate. (2): where enforcement "is stayed for any
-- period pending an appeal or for any other reason, an application shall not be made ... until the expiration of that period".
GIVEN `given by a Singapore court` IS A BOOLEAN, `the foreign country is one Part 1 applies to` IS A BOOLEAN, `the fee is paid` IS A BOOLEAN, `enforcement is stayed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registrar is to issue the certificate` IF
        `given by a Singapore court`
    AND `the foreign country is one Part 1 applies to`
    AND `the fee is paid`
    AND (NOT `enforcement is stayed`)
